{"availability":"available","full":"Yugo25/daytrading-entry-evaluator","name":"daytrading-entry-evaluator","description":"Evaluate the given entry point, based on the strategy.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-14T14:42:30Z","updated":"2026-10-09T18:31:49Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://yugo-daytrading-entry-evaluator.vercel.app","topics":["anthropic","claude-api","day-trading","forex","nextjs","postgresql","prisma","trading","trading-journal","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://yugo-daytrading-entry-evaluator.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:05.575Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:05.575Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:05.575Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T08:00:05.575Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An AI-powered tool that grades whether a day-trading entry setup complies with the rules of a written trading strategy, plus a trade journal and stats dashboard to go with it.","Upload a TradingView chart screenshot, and Claude (vision + structured output) scores the setup element-by-element against the strategy's own documentation, then renders a fixed-format report. You review the verdict, correct it when it's wrong, and those corrections become calibration examples for future evaluations.","Built for my own FX / gold day trading using two EMA-based strategies (20EMA and 200EMA). Deployed on Vercel and used from my phone as a PWA."],"features":["Chart evaluation – upload execution-timeframe (and optionally higher-timeframe) screenshots plus optional numeric prices; get a structured verdict in 1–3 minutes","Strategy-driven scoring – each strategy defines its own observation elements, scoring axes, ○/△/× element criteria, 5-level verdict labels and hard-cap special rules","Human-in-the-loop calibration – agree/disagree with each verdict, correct individual elements, and explain why; corrections are reused as few-shot examples","Trade journal – weekly journal pages (mirroring my Notion layout) with themes, reviews, rule-compliance tracking and a Notion CSV importer","Stats – P&L, win rate by strategy/session/pair, the rule-compliance × outcome quadrant, evaluator agreement rate, and a weak-spot map of which elements the evaluator gets corrected on most"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yugo25/daytrading-entry-evaluator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"db5438a128e030f80a6b1425cec4715a3dabe8f454282aca25a1983e7b7cdfbd","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:05.689Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:05.689Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An AI-powered tool that grades whether a day-trading entry setup complies with the rules of a written trading strategy, plus a trade journal and stats dashboard to go with it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yugo25/daytrading-entry-evaluator/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Built for my own FX / gold day trading using two EMA-based strategies (20EMA and 200EMA). Deployed on Vercel and used from my phone as a PWA.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yugo25/daytrading-entry-evaluator/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"db5438a128e030f80a6b1425cec4715a3dabe8f454282aca25a1983e7b7cdfbd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yugo25/daytrading-entry-evaluator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:05.689Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T18:31:49Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yugo25/daytrading-entry-evaluator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:05.690Z","hash":"db5438a128e030f80a6b1425cec4715a3dabe8f454282aca25a1983e7b7cdfbd","originalBytes":9356,"storedBytes":9356,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["strategy","journal","evaluation","src","docs","evaluator","stats","strategies","trade","blob","vercel","verdict","claude","criteria","lib","rules","add","ema","images","output"